quran[7]{c,v,t}:
  2,275,"Those who consume usury will not stand (on the Day of Resurrection) but like the one whom Satan has demented by his touch. That is because they say: ‘Trade is just like usury.’ But Allah has permitted trade and forbidden usury. On receiving a warning from his Lord, whoever stops (taking usury) shall keep (the gains of) whatever has passed. And his matter is in the hands of Allah. And those who go back (to usury) shall be the inhabitants of the Fire. They shall remain in it forever."
  2,276,Allah eliminates (blessings from) usury and makes charity flourish. Allah does not like any ingrate sinner.
  2,277,"Indeed, those who believe, perform righteous deeds, establish the prayer and give the alms-due shall have their reward with their Lord. There shall be no fear on them, nor shall they grieve."
  2,278,"O believers! Be God-conscious, and abandon (all claims to) what remains of usury if you are true believers."
  2,279,"If you do not (comply), then be warned of war from Allah and His Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him). If you repent, you will have your principal, neither doing wrong to others nor being wronged."
  2,280,"And if the debtor is in adversity, let there be respite until the time of ease. And if you remit (the debt) as an act of charity, it will be better for you if you know (the worth of generosity)."
  2,281,"And be cautious of the Day when you (all) shall be brought back to Allah. Then, every soul shall be recompensed fully for what it has earned—and they will not be wronged."
